+| 611 | ui.heading |  |  | `app` | History panel |
+| 612 | ui.text |  |  | `app` | The earlier return order begins the alternate-history route. The later order follows the historical timing: the original mission report (H6, p. 6-9) records western Pacific zone 3 as available on revolutions 6 and 7, with revolution 7 selected. On either route, the game's propellant warning, recovery tradeoff, crew-condition sequence, controllers' reactions, and next-mission constraints are dramatized; matching the timing does not make these consequences a reconstruction of the recovery. The post-flight stance and its relationship consequences are fictional. The historical opening — docking, the communications gap, the crew's stabilization of the spacecraft, the termination rule, and a western Pacific recovery — follows sources H1–H4. Once the earlier order activates ALTERNATE HISTORY, a later historical choice does not reset it. |
+| 613 | ui.hint |  |  | `app` | The status bar shows HISTORICAL CHOICE on a decision where one option matches the record, and ALTERNATE HISTORY once play has left it. Neither lamp is a recommendation. |
+| 614 | ui.text |  |  | `app` | Houston CAPCOM for Gemini VIII was Jim Lovell. His calls in the game are dramatized from the mission's air-ground transcript (H7); the crew's quoted words are from that transcript. |
