+| 833 | site.alt |  |  | `registry.site.bio.alt-01` | Dan Lee-Odinson at Kennedy Space Center, with the Vehicle Assembly Building behind him. |
+| 834 | site.label |  |  | `registry.site.bio.label-01` | DAN LEE-ODINSON / KENNEDY SPACE CENTER |
+| 835 | site.paragraph |  |  | `registry.site.bio.paragraph-01` | 03 / ABOUT THE DEV |
+| 836 | site.heading |  |  | `registry.site.bio.heading-01` | A lifelong dream. A new trajectory. |
+| 837 | site.paragraph |  |  | `registry.site.bio.paragraph-02` | I’m Dan Lee-Odinson, a Technical Project Manager and Space Studies student at Everglades University. |
+| 838 | site.paragraph |  |  | `registry.site.bio.paragraph-03` | My fascination with space began when I was six, holding my breath as Discovery’s STS-26 crew launched on the historic Return to Flight after the Challenger disaster. Watching Artemis II lift off in April 2026 turned that lifelong passion into a determination to be part of what comes next. |
